          "solution": "```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef purge_and_embargo_indices(t0, t1, test_start_idx: int, test_end_idx: int, embargo_bars: int) -> tuple[int, int, int, int]:\n    t0_arr = np.asarray(t0, dtype=int)\n    t1_arr = np.asarray(t1, dtype=int)\n    idx = np.arange(len(t0_arr))\n    test_idx = np.arange(test_start_idx, test_end_idx + 1)\n    test_t0_min = int(t0_arr[test_start_idx])\n    test_t1_max = int(t1_arr[test_idx].max())\n    cand = np.setdiff1d(idx, test_idx, assume_unique=True)\n    overlap_mask = (t0_arr[cand] <= test_t1_max) & (t1_arr[cand] >= test_t0_min)\n    n_purged = int(np.sum(overlap_mask))\n    after_purge = cand[~overlap_mask]\n    embargo_mask = (t0_arr[after_purge] > test_t1_max) & (t0_arr[after_purge] <= test_t1_max + embargo_bars)\n    n_embargoed = int(np.sum(embargo_mask))\n    clean_train = after_purge[~embargo_mask]\n    right_clean = clean_train[t0_arr[clean_train] > test_t1_max]\n    first_after = int(right_clean.min()) if len(right_clean) > 0 else -1\n    return (int(len(clean_train)), n_purged, n_embargoed, first_after)\n```"
